# DTF tier manifest: conda-remote-403-probe-fallback  (artifact-keeper#4929)
# Profile-set: filesystem + upstreams.mock-files (the oracle writes the
# channel's documents and forces per-path statuses at run time).
#
# #4904 (1.12.0) made a Remote's plain `repodata.json` fetch upstream `.zst`
# then `.bz2` and fall back to the plain `.json` only on 404. Three follow-ups
# (#4929), each asserted here against a real backend:
#   1. A channel on an S3 bucket without list permission answers 403 for the
#      `.zst`/`.bz2` it does not publish. The plain route (single Remote and a
#      Virtual's Remote member) must fall back to upstream's plain `.json`.
#   2. A channel that publishes `repodata.json.sig` signs its plain `.json`;
#      the plain route must serve those bytes, not the decoded `.zst`.
#   3. A Virtual member that reads an undecodable cached `.zst` evicts it, so
#      the next request refetches instead of failing until the entry expires.
#
# Red on 1.12.0 main before the fix (sha-8f4b018: the three FIX cases fail);
# the 1.11.x line never had the transcode, so cases 1 and 2 pass there.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-files"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
